# tally 2.1.8 R16 (the gate's rest 12), L §5.19, §8.4: an instance of x whose day is refused may fall on any day,
# as a hole day's, so bal(x, d) modelled is refused from the reading before it; after the reading of 2026-03-31 it
# reads again (960.00 PLN). refcore did so already; the engine answered 1 000.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input dd: int
input dv[m in months]: int
input fee: money PLN

move rent[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dd * dv[m] / dv[m])
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  fee = 30.00 PLN "s"
  dd = 20 "s"
  dv[2026-03] = 0 "s"
  dv[2026-04..2026-06] = 1 "s"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-02
  covers konto
  pad konto from world
  stated[konto] = 990.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end "saldo"

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-03-20)
ask q1: bal(konto, 2026-03-20) modelled
ask q2: bal(konto, 2026-04-20) modelled
=== expect
b: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-06-10
q1: refused: RUN-DIV division by zero
  cut 2026-06-10
q2: 960.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-10
